            <ArticleTitle>Epithelioid hemangioendothelioma of thoracic vertebra: a case report (2008: 11b).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>517-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00330-008-1035-5</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Epithelioid hemangioendothelioma is a rare, low-grade malignant hemangioendothelioma first reported in 1982. The disease is more likely to occur between 20 and 30 years with a 2:1 male-to-female ratio. Epithelioid hemangioendothelioma may occur in multiple organs and tissues, but it rarely involves the skeleton. We present a case in a thoracic vertebra.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
